      "message": "`remote_shared` backs every remote profile (`config_bb`, `config_gcp`, `remote_bb`, `remote21_bb`, `remote25_bb`), so this flips the download default for all remote builds and tests, not just release builds.\n\nVerified on RBE: `bazel build --config\u003dremote_bb --remote_download_minimal //:headless` succeeds (324 actions, 319 remote); the `.jars.txt` / `.entries.txt` manifests are on disk, but `bazel-bin/headless.war` is not.\n\nSo the agent already has everything it needs, and the 80 MB WAR download is pure overhead for jobs that don\u0027t consume it.\n\nSuggestion: keep `remote_shared --remote_download_minimal` and add an opt-in instead of flipping the default:\n\n`common:remote_toplevel --remote_download_outputs\u003dtoplevel`\n\nThe rare run that wants the artifact locally selects `--config\u003dremote_toplevel` (or add it constantly in `user.bazelrc`), and every CI job keeps today\u0027s behavior with no change — and no `remote_minimal` opt-out to remember and order correctly.",
